course: dictionary
lesson: 292
title: Amuse and its family
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Amuse is a verb, and it has a family of words: amused, amusing and amusement. To amuse someone is to make them laugh or smile. «It amuses you and it doesn't hurt me.» Here amuses means it makes you laugh or smile, because the speaker is saying the joke is fun for you but not hurtful to them.
explain: Amuse can also mean keeping someone busy and interested so they do not get bored, like keeping a baby amused with a toy. Check the clues in the sentence: is someone laughing, or just happily busy? Then try your meaning in the sentence to see if it still makes sense.
explain: Watch out for «not amused». It does not mean the same as amused. It means annoyed or displeased, so the words around it show a grumpy mood, not a happy one. Amusing means funny, and amusement is the enjoyment of being entertained, as at an amusement park.
fact: Amuse is a verb: amuse, amuses, amused, amusing.
fact: «Amuse» means to make someone laugh or smile.
fact: «Amuse» also means to keep someone busy and interested so they do not get bored.
fact: «Amusing» means funny, and «amusement» means fun or entertainment.
fact: «Not amused» means annoyed or displeased.
exercise: «It amuses you and it doesn't hurt me.» What does amuses mean here? | Ignores you | Hurts you badly | Makes you cry | *Makes you laugh or smile
exercise: The toy kept the baby ___ while we cooked dinner. Which word fits best? | amuses | *amused | amusing | amusement
exercise: «Dad was not amused when we ate the whole cake.» What does not amused mean? | *Annoyed | Sleepy | Hungry | Very happy
test: «The clown's jokes were very amusing.» What does amusing mean? | Strict | *Funny | Sad | Tired
test: «The family spent the day at the amusement park.» What does amusement mean here? | Hard work | *Fun and entertainment | Danger | Quiet rest
exam: Which word means to keep someone busy so they are not bored? | Scare | Bore | Annoy | *Amuse
